      "note": "Qwen 3.8 27B Q4 and Gemma 4 12B Q4 on a DGX Spark (NVIDIA GB10, Linux) with native 0.1.54: llama.cpp on CUDA, with MTP speculative decoding on by default for both models. 258 trials, three per model and scenario, ran October 28–30, 2026; none was repeated or replaced, and every raw verdict is kept. Three failures are set aside as infrastructure: one Linux script-sandbox failure and two gates the model wrote itself, which the harness classed as setup failures. Evaluation homes had package scripts switched off, so bug-fix-tdd, codemod-sweep and refactor-module could not pass for either model; without those 18 trials the developer failure rate is 0/21 for Qwen and 7/21 for Gemma. docblocks-theme-roundtrip lacked its DocBlocks tools in all six trials, and the harness stopped two Qwen route-multi trials and one Qwen author-fanout trial while they were still progressing. Task speeds are engine-log medians over every attempt. Memory is not shown: the GB10 shares its memory with the GPU in a way the measurement cannot see. Artifact reviews are by Claude Sonnet 4.6, one column per rubric. The six A/B readout reviews used a mismatched rubric and seven reviews graded a starting or incidental page instead of the work, so those 13 are excluded."
    }
